              ],
              "revised_value": "Opposed three Ukraine-assistance restrictions and supported one Ukraine-support authorization."
            },
            {
              "original_value_sha256": "f5f3b7b6c34e5797ad786c6778c11795e6c5028259396fbac1c37b3c4d331702",
              "path": [
                "relationship_basis",
                "semantic_relationship"
              ],
              "revised_value": "The accepted Ukraine, Jordan, and Taiwan choices generally preserve or authorize the bounded assistance at issue, while the accepted Israel choice supports a specific $3.3 billion FMF reduction; that country-specific contrast prevents a uniform cross-country conclusion."
            },
            {
              "original_value_sha256": "8ac091f367013059af351e3b4ef7c7029276e47a07c3ba54733dbdb2a2394fd7",
              "path": [
                "relationship_rationale"
              ],
              "revised_value": "The accepted semantic content—not proposition-relative direction labels—shows assistance-preserving or authorizing choices for Ukraine, Jordan, and Taiwan and a specific Israel FMF reduction choice. The contrast supports an interpretive boundary rather than a general pro-aid or anti-aid conclusion."
            },
            {
              "original_value_sha256": "c3f812961758d740b7f36af1437b98ccffee27d3abb9c7726ee401a14ebc2574",
              "path": [
                "material_limitations"
              ],
              "revised_value": [
                "The countries, accounts, measures, and restriction mechanisms differ.",
